`registerI18nEndpoints` only forwards `locale` to `protocol.getTranslations` and ignores optional request fields defined in the protocol schema (e.g. `namespace`, `keys`). This makes `/i18n/translations/:locale` incompatible with `GetTranslationsRequestSchema` and prevents clients from requesting scoped subsets of translations. Pass through supported query params (e.g. `req.query.namespace` and a parsed `req.query.keys`) when calling `getTranslations`.
```suggestion
                        const locale = req.params.locale;
                        const { namespace, keys } = req.query ?? {};

                        let parsedKeys: string[] | undefined;

                        if (Array.isArray(keys)) {
                            parsedKeys = keys.map((k) => String(k));
                        } else if (typeof keys === 'string' && keys.length > 0) {
                            let jsonParsed: unknown;
                            try {
                                jsonParsed = JSON.parse(keys);
                            } catch {
                                jsonParsed = undefined;
                            }

                            if (Array.isArray(jsonParsed)) {
                                parsedKeys = jsonParsed.map((k) => String(k));
                            } else {
                                parsedKeys = keys
                                    .split(',')
                                    .map((k) => k.trim())
                                    .filter((k) => k.length > 0);
                            }
                        }

                        const request: any = { locale };

                        if (typeof namespace === 'string' && namespace.length > 0) {
                            request.namespace = namespace;
                        }

                        if (parsedKeys && parsedKeys.length > 0) {
                            request.keys = parsedKeys;
                        }

                        const translations = await this.protocol.getTranslations(request);
```

The translations route is registered as `/i18n/translations/:locale`, but the ObjectStack client uses `/i18n/translations?locale=...` (and runtime HttpDispatcher supports both). As-is, RestServer-based deployments will 404 for the client’s default request shape. Consider registering the query-style route (and optionally keep `/:locale` as an alias) and accept `locale` from `req.query` when not present in the path.
```suggestion
        const translationsHandler = async (req: any, res: any) => {
            try {
                const localeFromParams = req && req.params ? req.params.locale : undefined;
                const localeFromQuery = req && req.query ? (req.query.locale as string | undefined) : undefined;
                const locale = localeFromParams ?? localeFromQuery;

                if (!locale) {
                    res.status(400).json({ error: 'Missing required "locale" parameter' });
                    return;
                }

                if (this.protocol.getTranslations) {
                    const translations = await this.protocol.getTranslations({ locale });
                    res.json(translations);
                } else {
                    res.status(501).json({ error: 'i18n service not available in protocol' });
                }
            } catch (error: any) {
                res.status(500).json({ error: error.message });
            }
        };

        // GET /i18n/translations?locale=... - Get translations for a locale (query style, default client shape)
        this.routeManager.register({
            method: 'GET',
            path: `${i18nPath}/translations`,
            handler: translationsHandler,
            metadata: {
                summary: 'Get translations for a locale',
                tags: ['i18n'],
            },
        });

